<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Narendra Modi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1950">1950</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Narendra Modi (born 1950) is an Indian politician of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bharatiya-janata-party">Bharatiya Janata Party</a> who has been prime minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> since 2014. Previously chief minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> from 2001 to 2014, a period that included the communal violence of 2002, he led his party to the first single-party majority in thirty years in 2014 and won again in 2019 and 2024, the last time relying on coalition partners.</p></div>
